---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Toc from '../components/Toc.astro';
import Mark from '../components/Mark.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Ladder from '../components/Ladder.astro';
import { app } from '../lib/links';
const SECTIONS: [string, string][] = [['search', 'When you search'], ['save', 'When you save or watch'], ['employers', 'What employers can’t see'], ['decisions', 'Five separate decisions'], ['sharing', 'When you share'], ['change', 'Changing your mind'], ['site', 'This website'], ['claims', 'What we don’t claim']];
---
<Base title="How your privacy works at Linkbot"
  description="What happens to what you type, save and share on Linkbot: searches aren’t stored, and nothing reaches an employer without your decision."
  path="/privacy" crumbs={[['How your privacy works', '/privacy']]}>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">How your privacy works</p>
      <h1><span class="h1-line">Private by default.</span> <span class="h1-line h1-soft">Shared only when you decide.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">No lock icons and no absolute promises. Here is what Linkbot does with what you type, save and share, what it never does, and where the limits are.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap doc">
    <Toc items={SECTIONS} label="On this page" />
    <div class="doc-body">
      <section id="search" aria-labelledby="search-title">
        <h2 id="search-title">When you search without an account</h2>
        <ul class="marks">
          <li><Mark tone="fit" size={14} /><div><b>Your words are read in your browser.</b><p>Linkbot turns them into criteria on your device. To search, it sends the criteria it understood (the phrases you see under the search field), not your whole sentence. Words that might be a place are looked up one at a time.</p></div></li>
          <li><Mark tone="fit" size={14} /><div><b>Nothing is stored.</b><p>A search without an account writes nothing to Linkbot’s database. Linkbot’s own records of a search are counts only, such as how many criteria and how many results: never your words, places or results.</p></div></li>
          <li><Mark tone="fit" size={14} /><div><b>Nobody is told.</b><p>Searching and viewing listings send nothing to any employer.</p></div></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="save" aria-labelledby="save-title">
        <h2 id="save-title">When you save a job or watch a search</h2>
        <p>Keeping anything needs an account, so it has a private place to live. You sign in first, and you confirm what to keep after signing in; nothing is saved before that.</p>
        <ul class="marks">
          <li><Mark tone="fit" size={14} /><div><b>Only you can see it.</b><p>Saved jobs and watched directions are private to your account. There is no public profile.</p></div></li>
          <li><Mark tone="tradeoff" size={14} /><div><b>Linkbot reads what it works on.</b><p>To watch a direction for you, Linkbot’s servers read it and compare it with new listings. That is the work you asked for. It isn’t end-to-end encrypted, and we don’t say it is.</p></div></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="employers" aria-labelledby="employers-title">
        <h2 id="employers-title">What employers can’t see</h2>
        <ul class="marks">
          <li><Mark tone="unknown" size={14} /><div><b>No directory of people.</b><p>Employers can’t search for you or browse profiles. There aren’t any.</p></div></li>
          <li><Mark tone="unknown" size={14} /><div><b>Not your searches, saves or watches.</b><p>None of it is visible to any employer, and no employer can see who saved a job.</p></div></li>
          <li><Mark tone="unknown" size={14} /><div><b>Not your matches.</b><p>A match is not a disclosure, not a sign of interest and not permission to contact you. Matching never applies for you.</p></div></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="decisions" aria-labelledby="decisions-title">
        <h2 id="decisions-title">Five separate decisions</h2>
        <p>Finding a job, matching it, keeping it, sharing details and applying are five separate steps. None of them happens because another one did, and each says who can see what.</p>
        <Ladder />
      </section>

      <section id="sharing" aria-labelledby="sharing-title">
        <h2 id="sharing-title">When you decide to share</h2>
        <p>Sharing is always a separate step you confirm, for one named recipient, with exactly the details you choose. Before anything is sent, you see which details go to whom.</p>
        <div class="two">
          <div class="mode"><h3>Once</h3><p>You confirm one share of chosen details with one recipient.</p></div>
          <div class="mode"><h3>By standing rule</h3><p>You set a rule: these details, to this named recipient, for this long. Linkbot shares under it without asking each time. You create it explicitly; Linkbot never creates one for you.</p></div>
        </div>
        <ul class="marks">
          <li><Mark tone="fit" size={14} /><div><b>A receipt every time.</b><p>Who received which details, when, and under which choice. Your history stays visible to you.</p></div></li>
          <li><Mark tone="fit" size={14} /><div><b>Applying is separate too.</b><p>An application sends only the details you confirm. Names and contact details are not part of an application to a company on Linkbot.</p></div></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="status-line"><span class="status" data-tone="built"><Mark tone="tradeoff" size={10} />Built, tested in staging; not yet live with employers</span></p>
      </section>

      <section id="change" aria-labelledby="change-title">
        <h2 id="change-title">Changing your mind</h2>
        <ul class="marks">
          <li><Mark tone="fit" size={14} /><div><b>Pause, edit or close a watched direction.</b><p>Paused means no checks. Linkbot also asks you to review a watched direction regularly, and it ends after 90 days.</p></div></li>
          <li><Mark tone="fit" size={14} /><div><b>Revoke a standing rule or access you gave.</b><p>It stops access from that moment on.</p></div></li>
          <li><Mark tone="unknown" size={14} /><div><b>What revoking can’t do.</b><p>Copies a recipient already received aren’t recalled, and the receipts of what was shared stay in your history. We say this up front so revoking means exactly what it says.</p></div></li>
        </ul>
        <p><a class="link" href={app('#/privacy')}>Open Privacy &amp; sharing in Linkbot<Icon name="arrow" /></a></p>
      </section>

      <section id="site" aria-labelledby="site-title">
        <h2 id="site-title">This website</h2>
        <ul class="plain">
          <li>No cookies, no analytics, no third-party trackers. The typeface is served from this site.</li>
          <li>When you search from here, your words travel to Linkbot in the part of the address after “#”, which browsers never send to a server. Linkbot reads them once and removes them from the address.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="claims" aria-labelledby="claims-title">
        <h2 id="claims-title">What we don’t claim</h2>
        <p>Linkbot is built to be private by default and to share only with permission. That is different from saying nobody can ever see anything. So we don’t claim end-to-end encryption, zero-knowledge processing, anonymous matching or that Linkbot can’t see your data, and we don’t promise perfect matches.</p>
        <h3>Principles we hold ourselves to</h3>
        <ul class="plain">
          <li>The core service for individuals stays free.</li>
          <li>We don’t sell personal information.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-hero { padding-block: clamp(40px, 7vw, 88px) clamp(32px, 5vw, 56px); }
  .page-hero .wrap { display: grid; gap: 20px; justify-items: center; text-align: center; }
  .page-hero .lede { text-wrap: balance; }
  .page-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 1.1rem + 3.9vw, 4.75rem); max-width: 17ch; }
  .h1-line { display: block; }
  .h1-soft { font-weight: 300; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .doc { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 32px clamp(40px, 6vw, 96px); padding-bottom: var(--band); }
  @media (min-width: 64rem) { .doc { grid-template-columns: 15rem minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  .doc-body { display: grid; gap: var(--space-section); max-width: 48rem; }
  .doc-body, .doc-body section { min-width: 0; }
  .doc-body section { display: grid; gap: 16px; scroll-margin-top: 96px; }
  .doc-body h2 { font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 1.35rem + 1.4vw, 2.4rem); }
  .doc-body p { color: var(--ink-2); }
  .marks { display: grid; gap: 0; border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); }
  .marks li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 14px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 14px; align-items: baseline; padding: 14px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .marks li :global(.mark) { position: relative; top: 2px; }
  .marks b { font-weight: 650; }
  .marks p { margin-top: 4px; font-size: var(--size-small); }
  .two { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 12px; }
  @media (max-width: 36rem) { .two { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  .mode { display: grid; gap: 6px; padding: 18px; border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: var(--r-3); }
  .mode p { font-size: var(--size-small); }
  .plain { display: grid; gap: 8px; padding-left: 1.1em; list-style: disc; color: var(--ink-2); }
  .status-line { display: flex; }
</style>
